url: 'https://kokkos.org'
abstract: >-
  Kokkos Kernels implements local computational kernels for
  linear algebra and graph operations, using the Kokkos
  shared-memory parallel programming model. "Local" means
  not using MPI, or running within a single MPI process
  without knowing about MPI. "Computational kernels" are
  coarse-grained operations, consisting of substantial work 
  suitable for on-node parallel execution using Kokkos. Kokkos
  Kernels can be the building block of a parallel linear
  algebra library that uses MPI and threads for parallelism,
  or it can be used stand-alone in your application.
